Skill	craft:github
Bash	cd <craft>/skills/github && wc -c take-in.md tracker.md && cat take-in.md
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; bash $D/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91; echo "exit=$?"; git remote -v; gh auth status 2>&1 | head -3
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; bash $D/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91; echo "exit=$?"; gh repo view --json nameWithOwner 2>&1 | head -2
text	I could not take #91 into work. I stopped at the first step.  **What happened** - The issue check script failed twice with `HTTP 502: Bad Gateway (https://api.github.com/graphql)`. `gh repo view` failed with the same error. - Because the check failed, I did not read the issue. I have no title or summary for #91. - Nothing changed: no worktree, no branch, no assignment and no edits.  **A second problem, separate from the 502** This checkout's only remote, `origin`, is a local path (`…/tmp.QV20MbbzL2/down.origin`), not a GitHub URL. Even after GitHub recovers, `gh` may not know which repository #91 belongs to.  **What you can do** - If the 502 is a GitHub outage, wait and send `#91` again. - If #91 is in a particular GitHub repository, send its full URL (`https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/issues/91`). That avoids the local-remote problem.
